# Per-user Claude state (machine-local; not for the repo)
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
/apps/desktop/target/

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Build / runtime artifacts (paths anticipated by the design notes)
# CLAUDE.md section 5 describes the WHOLE of var/ as the gitignored data tree,
# but this pattern only ever covered var/arxmcp/ -- so ingest staging trees
# (var/fourier-staging/, var/textbook-staging/, ~93 MB of source PDFs) and the
# loose driver scripts beside them showed up as untracked noise on every
# status, and were one `git add .` away from being committed. Widened to all
# of var/ to match the documented intent. Nothing under var/ has ever been
# tracked (`git ls-files var/` is empty), so this changes no history.
/var/
*.log
*.egg-info/

# E11_S05 — restic creds. The .template is committed; the filled
# file with the operator's RESTIC_REPOSITORY / B2 creds is not.
ops/restic-env.sh

# E13_S06 — SBOM JSON outputs. The raw CycloneDX files are multi-MB
# and timestamped per run; the audit doc references the procedure
# (``make sbom``) rather than committing the artifacts directly.
# A future release-tag milestone may flip this to commit only the
# tag's signed SBOM.
.claude/docs/security/sbom/*.json
.claude/docs/security/sbom/*.cdx.json

# Codex (OpenAI agent tool) working artifacts — ephemeral, per-session scratch.
# arXMCP's agent instructions live in CLAUDE.md; these are local codex state and
# must not enter git. `.agents/` showed up as a stray, divergent skill mirror
# (NOT written by sync-repos.py, which targets .claude/skills/); `.codex/` is the
# codex session dir.
#
# AGENTS.md: DECIDED for arXMCP (2026-07-29) — ignore it. It was previously left
# "tracked-eligible, decide per-repo". Reasons to ignore here: (a) CLAUDE.md § 1
# restricts the repo root to eight named files and AGENTS.md is not one of them;
# (b) this repo's agent instructions are CLAUDE.md, so a second 35 KB root
# instruction file is a duplicate that will drift out of sync with it;
# (c) `.codex/` is already ignored, so the rest of the codex surface is local
# state and AGENTS.md is the same class. The fleet is deliberately NOT uniform on
# this — proclivity tracks its AGENTS.md and that stays correct for proclivity;
# the per-repo choice is the point.
.agents/
.codex/
AGENTS.md

# Milestone-pipeline concurrency lock — a live PID:milestone:timestamp record
# written by milestone-pipeline-init-state.sh while a milestone holds the
# pipeline. Pure runtime state: it names a process on THIS box, it is stale the
# moment that process exits, and committing it would hand every clone a lock
# referring to a PID that never existed there. Left on disk (deleting it mid-run
# would let a second session start concurrently) and out of git.
.claude/notes/milestones/.lock
